   "notes": "Described the GPT-2-style decoder models (Table: Model configurations used for GPT-2). Primary config is the smallest, 355M. The 8.3B model is the headline model. The paper also trains BERT-style encoders with rearranged layer norm (336M/1.3B/3.9B, vocab 30522); these are not described here. The scaling-study table (1.2B-8.3B, head dim 96) is a throughput study; its 8.3B uses 32 heads versus 24 in the trained 8.3B. The paper defers the remaining details to GPT-2 ('refer to the original papers'), but it never restates them. Positional embedding type, layernorm eps, biases, d_ff, kv heads, attention scale and the GeLU approximation form are therefore left not_stated, and no ancestor values are filled in. Whether a final layernorm precedes the head is not stated, so it is omitted. Activation is recorded as 'gelu' because the paper says GeLU and cites the GeLU paper. Whether the exact or tanh form is used is not stated. The vocab of 51200 is the padded size given in the scaling section (original 50257)."
